From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH] Drop dead `import os` from anaconda_options.py

The current scons option validator iterates the options template's
namespace and rejects every name that is not a whitelisted escript
option.  `import os` (and the duplicate `openmp = True`) are leftovers
with no consumer in this file, so the build aborts with
"Unknown option 'os'" before anything compiles.

Upstream fix: https://github.com/LutzGross/esys-escript.github.io/commit/b18b2421b
---
 scons/templates/anaconda_options.py | 3 ---
 1 file changed, 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/scons/templates/anaconda_options.py b/scons/templates/anaconda_options.py
index 7cfef5d23..83d59763e 100644
--- a/scons/templates/anaconda_options.py
+++ b/scons/templates/anaconda_options.py
@@ -16,9 +16,6 @@
 # Refer to README_FIRST for usage instructions.

 escript_opts_version = 203
-openmp = True
-
-import os

 openmp=1
 paso=1
